# Implementation report

Baseline implementation/evidence commit: `83a0ad4351300e4537435ce637a995207e221ed0`. Original task: `../handoff-20260920.md`; user-authorized corrections: `plan-correction.md`. Root is the final exclusive writer. The implementation worker completed and stopped before Root host acceptance.

P1-B implements the user-approved report-submission-only capability: registered `planner-report-only`, empty declared tools, no inherited project/global context or skills, no nested subagents, one structured result call via `{hard:1, block:"*"}`. Missing registration refuses before REQUEST. Ordinary requests omit this budget. The exact budget, capability binding and raw public terminal are persisted.

The correction grant comes from durable Task state. Worker/explorer repair links to the immutable original execution; validator/reviewer cannot bypass it, and a second concurrent consumer refuses before dispatch. The child receives the stored spec, typed report material and Root origin evidence. It contributes no new Truth paths. Accepted declaration corrections resolve only declaration finding evidence; final acceptance still requires review. A second malformed report blocks. A report-only budget terminal has a separate failure family.

The final Root correction makes both truth/comparison readOnly semantics and predecessor exclusion use the immutable origin identity. It precedes the passing full release.

Production changes: `delegate.ts`, `index.ts`, `types.ts`, `ledger-store.ts`, `request-events.ts`; tests: `p1-delegation.test.mjs`, `delegate.test.mjs`; domain/docs: `CONTEXT.md`, both READMEs, ADR-0009, capability matrix. ADR-0008 and measurement closure are updated from P3 evidence separately.

Final correction adds `evidence.ts` and `orchestrate.ts`: report-only comparisons against the immutable origin now preserve over-declared/missing findings, and final verdict reliability checks those arrays directly. `truth-hardening-red.log` reproduces acceptance of a fabricated unchanged path before the fix; `truth-hardening-test-p1.log` and `truth-hardening-typecheck.log` pass afterward. New plugin-entry regressions cover both absent and pre-existing unchanged fabricated paths and retain the successful repair case. No existing assertions were replaced.

The first full release after hardening (`release-run-ZrJioW`, exit 1) exposed two legacy `evidence.test.mjs` expectations that explicitly permitted this report-only bypass. Root strengthened them: `unexplained:false` becomes `true`, and action `review` becomes `revalidate` when no origin/prior truth exists. Both assertions remain, now enforcing rejection, and a new positive control proves a real cumulative prior basis still proceeds to review. `assertion-audit.json` records the exact two replacements; no assertion was dropped or weakened.

Version provenance: the 27-row P3 run `study-run-yL4RzS` and TUI matrix predate only this last declaration-hardening change. The exact pre-fix source diff/hashes are preserved in `pre-truth-hardening.patch` and `pre-truth-hardening-source.json`. The measurements describe the frozen build in each run, not a byte-identical final build. None of the P3 REQUESTs carries a report-only budget; the new malformed-declaration path has dedicated current-entry regression evidence and a subsequent complete release. The capability definition and TUI cancellation controller were unchanged by hardening.

Checks: worker typecheck/test:p1/diff-check exit 0 (`p1b-r2-*`); final full normal-terminal release exit 0 (`../release-run-ysqfcU/`); real capability probe PASS (`../report-only-run-3zZ7ry/`); three real TUI scenarios PASS, independently checked (`host-validation.md`). Harness checks include aggregation, model-identity accounting, actual TUI proof predicates and slot-audit gating. The initial added identity-test variable collision and its corrected passing run are both retained in `harness-run-*.log`.

Superseding final checks after declaration hardening and strengthened legacy expectations: `../release-run-GurHBj` is full `npm run test:release` exit 0; `harness-run-20260920T094955Z.log` is current harness exit 0. The earlier ysqfcU pass remains historical for the prior code. Independent P3 recomputation is in measurement-validation.md; all 27 measured rows are quality/identity passing, with no report-only execution in those paths.

